    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the repo, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a successful owner create emit an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger containing the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\nI made two changes:\n\n1. **New function** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`:\n   ```java\n   audit.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n           owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n   It reads the persisted owner via `@Val Owner` (so the id is already assigned by `SaveOwner`).\n\n2. **Wired it into** `owners.POST.yml` as a new `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, carrying the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as its neighbors.\n\nPlacing it after `save` guarantees the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate are all populated. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test passes (the captured line was `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-10`), and the build is green.",
